# qkt minimal project

This project was generated by `qkt create template --kind minimal`.

It starts a QKT daemon without a broker. Use it for local strategy development,
paper-only flows, and as the smallest base for adding your own broker wiring.

Read `CONFIG.md` for a plain-English explanation of `.env`,
`docker-compose.yml`, `qkt.config.yaml`, state, and local strategy deployment.

## First Run

```bash
cp .env.example .env
docker compose --env-file .env config --quiet
make up
make status
```

## Environment Values

The generated defaults are enough for a first local run:

```dotenv
QKT_IMAGE_TAG=v{{QKT_VERSION}}
QKT_STARTING_BALANCE=10000
```

`QKT_IMAGE_TAG` selects the QKT Docker image. `QKT_STARTING_BALANCE` is the
local account balance used by the generated config.

Keep `.env` out of Git.

## Commands

Use these commands from the project directory:

```bash
make up                         # start the QKT daemon
make logs                       # tail daemon logs
make status                     # show deployed strategies
make deploy STRAT=ema_cross     # deploy strategies/ema_cross.qkt
make resync-dry-run STRAT=ema_cross
make resync STRAT=ema_cross
make reconcile STRAT=ema_cross
make stop STRAT=ema_cross
make down                       # stop containers without deleting state
```

## Strategy Flow

1. Edit or add a `.qkt` file in `strategies/`.
2. Run `make up`.
3. Deploy with `make deploy STRAT=<name>`.
4. For edits, run `make resync-dry-run`, then `make resync`, then `make reconcile`.

This scaffold has no live broker route by default.

